---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Copyright and permissions">
  <div class="wrap" style="padding-top:40px">
    <div class="prose" style="font-family:var(--sans); font-size:17px">
      <h1 style="font-size:40px; margin-bottom:0.5em">Copyright and permissions</h1>
      <p>Every work in the archive is marked with one of three statuses:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Public domain</strong>: the work’s copyright has expired, and the text is hosted here. Translations carry their own copyright, so a translation is hosted only if it is also in the public domain or used with permission.</li>
        <li><strong>Published with permission</strong>: the author, estate or publisher has given written permission for the archive to host the text.</li>
        <li><strong>Link to free copy</strong>: the work is in copyright but freely available from its publisher or author; the archive describes it and links to that copy.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>For authors, estates and publishers</h2>
      <p>If you hold the rights to a work and would like it hosted, please write to <a href="mailto:permissions@islamicarchives.org">permissions@islamicarchives.org</a>. Permission can be limited (for example, to online reading only, or to particular works), and is acknowledged on every page where the work appears.</p>
      <h2 id="takedown">Takedown requests</h2>
      <p>If you believe a work has been published here without the right to do so, write to <a href="mailto:permissions@islamicarchives.org?subject=Takedown%20request">permissions@islamicarchives.org</a> with the page address and the basis of your claim. The work will be taken offline promptly while the request is reviewed.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
